Run /start-session at the beginning of every new session
Run /self-review before pushing your branch
Keep files under 250 lines (TS/TSX) or 400 lines (Go) or 300 lines (C#)
One exported component per file -- extract sub-components
Barrel exports (index.ts) are the public API of every module
Tests live next to source: foo.ts -> foo.test.ts, foo.go -> foo_test.go
No god files: utils.ts, helpers.ts, common.ts -- name things specifically
Conventional Commits: feat(scope): description
Never skip hooks with --no-verify -- fix the underlying issue
Read before writing. Understand context before editing.
Use targeted searches before reading entire files
Small focused changes. One concern per commit. One concern per PR.
Mock at boundaries only: HTTP, DB, third-party APIs. Never mock internals.
Update SESSION_LOG.md after meaningful work -- future you will thank you
Run /sync-docs after locked decisions to keep docs consistent
{{#ifMultiTenancy config}}
Every tenant-scoped query MUST filter by tenant_id. No exceptions.
{{/ifMultiTenancy}}
{{#ifHasStack config "next-ssr"}}
Default to Server Components. Only add "use client" when you need interactivity.
{{/ifHasStack}}
{{#ifHasStack config "go"}}
context.Context is always the first parameter. Errors are always wrapped with context.
{{/ifHasStack}}
Derive state during render -- never useEffect to sync state between variables
Use /plan-review to challenge your plan before writing code
Use /adr to document decisions you will forget in 3 months
